Verdict: NOT_SUPPORTED
Rationale: The claim states that the 2004 World Series of Poker gold bracelet holder held the Commissioner position in the 2011 competition where Michael McDonald was the youngest person to win an event. The evidence shows that Annie Duke was the Commissioner in 2011 and that she won the 2004 gold bracelet. However, the evidence contradicts the claim that Michael McDonald was the youngest person to win an event in 2011. The finding explicitly states 'No' to this part of the claim, citing that McDonald won a tournament in 2011 outside the World Series of Poker (Epic Poker League). Therefore, the claim is not supported due to this contradiction.
Rounds: 2, findings: 4
